<template>
  <Teleport to="body">
    <dialog ref="dialog" class="view-dialog public-views-info-dialog" :class="{'is-museum':museum,'gallery-dialog-veil':museum,'is-note':note,'is-centred':centred,'is-dark':dark,'is-closing':closing}" :style="viewportStyle" :aria-labelledby="note ? undefined : 'public-views-info-title'" :aria-label="note ? 'Henry’s note' : undefined" aria-describedby="public-views-info-copy" @cancel.prevent="leave('close')" @keydown.stop>
      <header class="view-dialog-head">
        <h2 v-if="!note" id="public-views-info-title"><GalleryMark v-if="museum"/>{{ museum ? 'The View Gallery' : 'About Views' }}</h2>
        <GalleryDesignLink v-if="museum && !note" class="public-views-design-entry" @design="openDesign"/>
        <button ref="close" type="button" class="view-dialog-close" aria-label="Close dialog" @click="leave('close')">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m5 5 10 10M15 5 5 15" /></svg>
        </button>
      </header>
      <ViewAboutContent v-if="note" id="public-views-info-copy" :article="!museum" @design="openDesign" @project="leave('close')"/>
      <div v-else-if="museum" id="public-views-info-copy" class="public-views-info-copy gallery-introduction">
        <p>A <AiViewTerm /> connects Henry’s work, ideas and experiences around a visitor’s question. The Gallery brings these readings together as exhibitions you can step inside and explore.</p>
        <p><strong>Browse</strong> previews the exhibitions. Choose one, then enter it through the <strong>Entrance</strong>. <strong>Create</strong> lets AI build your own exhibition around your perspective on Henry. <strong>Archive</strong> lets you browse Henry’s original material.</p>
      </div>
      <div v-else id="public-views-info-copy" class="public-views-info-copy">
        <p>Each <AiViewTerm /> begins with a visitor&rsquo;s question or perspective. AI brings together Henry&rsquo;s work, ideas and experiences, then composes a narrative around the connections it finds.</p>
        <p>The Gallery gives that reading a physical form. Its rooms place the narrative beside the original sources that support it. The same <AiViewTerm /> is also available as an article.</p>
        <p>The collection gathers <AiViewTerm plural /> that visitors have chosen to make public. Visitors can follow their questions through the Gallery and leave a note after the exhibition.</p>
      </div>
      <div v-if="museum && !note" class="gallery-info-media">
        <div class="gallery-info-media-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Explore the Gallery">
          <button v-for="(item,index) in mediaTabs" :id="`gallery-info-tab-${item.id}`" :key="item.id" type="button" role="tab" :aria-selected="media===item.id" :tabindex="media===item.id?0:-1" :aria-controls="`gallery-info-panel-${item.id}`" @click="selectMedia(item.id)" @keydown="mediaKey($event,index)">{{ item.label }}</button>
        </div>
        <div class="gallery-info-media-panels">
        <div id="gallery-info-panel-film" class="gallery-info-media-panel" :class="{'is-selected':media==='film'}" :inert="media!=='film'" :aria-hidden="media!=='film'" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="gallery-info-tab-film">
          <GalleryFilm :dark="dark" :active="media==='film' && !closing" />
        </div>
        <div id="gallery-info-panel-plan" class="gallery-info-media-panel" :class="{'is-selected':media==='plan'}" :inert="media!=='plan'" :aria-hidden="media!=='plan'" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="gallery-info-tab-plan">
          <MuseumFloorPlan :area="area" :dark="dark" @navigate="leave('navigate',$event)"/>
        </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <button v-if="museum && !note && tourAvailable" class="public-views-tour" type="button" @click="leave('tour')"><span>Take the Gallery tour</span><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="8"/><path d="m8 6.5 5 3.5-5 3.5Z"/></svg></button>
      <p v-if="!note && !museum" class="public-views-info-removal">To remove a <AiViewTerm /> you&rsquo;ve shared, <a href="mailto:whenry6688@gmail.com?subject=Public%20View%20removal">email Henry</a> with its link.</p>
